<section class="mb-section mb-section-cream-2">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row g-4 g-lg-5">
            <div class="col-lg-8">
                <div class="mb-prose">
                    <h2>Who we are</h2>
                    <p>
                        Sabarna is a small food business registered in West Bengal, India, operating from
                        Village Sabarna, P.O. Kharagpur 721301. "We" and "us" below mean that business.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Prices and payment</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>All prices are in Indian Rupees (₹) and include GST where it applies.</li>
                        <li>We accept UPI, credit cards, debit cards and netbanking. <strong>We do not accept cash on delivery.</strong></li>
                        <li>An order is confirmed only after the payment is authorised. A parcel is never dispatched on a promise to pay.</li>
                        <li>We may correct an obvious pricing error before dispatch and refund you in full if you do not accept the corrected price.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h2>Stock and batches</h2>
                    <p>
                        Everything is made in small batches, so a product can go out of stock without notice.
                        Adding a jar to your basket does not reserve it; the stock is taken when the order is paid.
                        If two people pay for the last jar at once, the first payment wins and the second is
                        refunded immediately with an apology.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Delivery</h2>
                    <p>
                        Timelines, courier partners and the free-shipping threshold are described on our
                        <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Shipping">shipping page</a>, which forms part of
                        these terms. Address details are your responsibility — a parcel returned for a wrong
                        address is re-shipped at cost.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Food, allergens and shelf life</h2>
                    <p>
                        Our products are made in a home-style kitchen that also handles milk, mustard, chilli
                        and peanuts. If you have a severe allergy, please write to us before ordering and we
                        will tell you exactly what shares the kitchen that week.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Reviews and content</h2>
                    <p>
                        Photographs on this site are of our own jars and kitchen. Descriptive words such as
                        "grainy" or "smoky" describe what we taste — they are not a guarantee that every palate
                        will agree.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Using this website</h2>
                    <p>
                        Please do not attempt to break, scrape or overload this website. The admin area is for
                        staff only. We may refuse or cancel an order where we believe there has been fraud or abuse.
                    </p>

                    <h2>Governing law</h2>
                    <p>
                        These terms are governed by Indian law, and any dispute will be heard by the courts
                        of Kolkata, West Bengal.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4">
                <aside class="mb-note-card mb-note-card-sticky">
                    <h2 class="mb-note-title">Three things worth knowing</h2>
                    <ul class="mb-note-list">
                        <li>Prices include GST.</li>
                        <li>Online payment only — no cash on delivery.</li>
                        <li>Stock is taken when the payment succeeds, not when you add to basket.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <a class="btn btn-outline-brand btn-sm mt-2" asp-controller="Contact" asp-action="Index">Ask about these terms</a>
                </aside>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
